This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by any hardware or software vendor.  It contains no vendor
firmware, binaries, libraries, fonts or decompilation output.  To run a program you supply your own copy of it and
of the files it needs, which you must be entitled to use.  tests/run-examples.sh downloads Lua, SQLite and zlib
from their official sites for testing; they are not part of this distribution.

Some techniques follow 3dsrecomp (https://github.com/fearkov/3dsrecomp), licensed MIT as declared in its Cargo.toml:
the changed-register dataflow of the emitter's --locals-changed mode (after 3dsrecomp's src/codegen/locals.rs,
reimplemented in C++ in repo/patches/a64port-recomp.patch), the address-table and code-pointer heuristics of code
discovery in a64recomp.cpp, and treating any two NaNs as equal when verifying leaves.  Its licence notice:

